        <section class="legal-section">
          <span class="legal-kicker">What Cookies Do Here</span>
          <h2>They help the site work better for visitors.</h2>
          <p>Seascape Vacations uses cookies and similar browser storage to support browsing, remember lightweight site state such as whether an email popup was already shown, and keep direct-booking paths measurable.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <span class="legal-kicker">Traffic Readback</span>
          <h3>GA4 and Seascape events measure the site.</h3>
          <p>The site uses Google Analytics 4 and Seascape's own conversion events to understand page visits, direct-booking clicks, email signups, and owner inquiry actions. Meta Pixel has been removed, and the site does not use PostHog.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <span class="legal-kicker">Consent</span>
          <h3>Your browser controls are still available.</h3>
          <p>You can block or clear cookies in your browser settings. Some site preferences or measurement signals may not work the same way after cookies or browser storage are cleared.</p>
        </section>
